    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (76.16) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08), our two strongest plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Freddy Peralta; despite a slight park penalty, his elite spot in the order and the high probability of stolen base opportunities\u2014fueled by Peralta\u2019s slow delivery\u2014make him a mandatory start. **Jacob Wilson** faces a favorable encounter against Bradford, where he leverages a 19% SP skill advantage and a 10% park boost to reach his elite scoring tier. **Jackson Merrill** also provides strong value (69.57) against Bibee, capitalizing on a dynamic platoon edge that elevates his profile well above the marginal threshold.\n\nThe decision to bench **Coby Mayo** (43.08) was the closest call of the morning. While **Coby Mayo** possesses power upside, his late-order placement and negative platoon splits against Peralta pushed him just below the utility floor held by **Kyle Tucker** (51.47). Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with several bats facing elite arms: **Heliot Ramos** (44.53) and **Andy Pages** (47.54) both face Henderson, whose sub-3.00 xERA limits their output. Despite this, **Heliot Ramos** remains a factor in our strategy due to the 85% SB success rate tied to the opposing battery, keeping him viable as a speed-focused play. \n\nManagers should remain alert regarding the status of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (54.82) and **Drake Baldwin** (54.77). Both are currently hitting in the 54-point range, sitting just inside the \"Marginal\" to \"Strong\" transition zone. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** enjoys a 14% boost from his platoon matchup against Cease, the low xERA of the opposing starter introduces a degree of volatility that could suppress counting stats. We are monitoring all lineups for late scratches, but as it stands, we are prioritizing high-volume order positions like those held by **Sam Antonacci** and **Drake Baldwin** to maximize our daily run-scoring potential. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, requiring us to extract every point of efficiency from our active roster to maintain our competitive stance in the Roto standings.",
